ue,"_score_insider_own":43.7,"_gate_insider_buying":0.0,"_gp_insider_buying":false,"_score_insider_buying":0.0,"pf":[],"description_full":"MACOM Technology Solutions Holdings, Inc., together with its subsidiaries, provides analog semiconductor solutions for use in wireless and wireline applications across the radio frequency (RF), microwave, millimeter wave, and lightwave spectrum. The company offers a portfolio of standard and custom devices, including integrated circuits, multi-chip modules, diodes, amplifiers, switches and switch limiters, passive and active components, and subsystems. Its semiconductor products are electronic components that are incorporated in electronic systems, such as wireless base stations, optical networks, radar and medical systems, satellite networks, and test and measurement applications. The company serves carrier infrastructure, which comprise long-haul/metro, 5G and 6G infrastructure, satellite communications, and fiber-to-the-X/passive optical network; industrial and defense, including military and commercial radar, RF jammers, electronic countermeasures, and communication data links, as well as multi-market applications, such as industrial, medical, test and measurement, and scientific applications; and data centers. It sells its products through direct sales force, applications engineering staff, independent sales representatives, resellers, and distributors. The company operates in the United States, China, Japan, Singapore, South Korea, Taiwan, and internationally. MACOM Technology Solutions Holdings, Inc. was formerly known as M/A-Com Technology Solutions Holdings, Inc. and changed its name to MACOM Technology Solutions Holdings, Inc. in 2016. MACOM Technology Solutions Holdings, Inc. was founded in 1950 and is based in Lowell, Massachusetts.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Stephen G. Daly | President, CEO & Chairman | Age 59 | Compensation: $2.0M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 2K people. Revenue per employee of $484K ranks in the above the sector median among Technology peers, improving at 9%/yr \u2014 growing workforce leverage. Each employee generates $96K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $40K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 4\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags low compensation governance risk (1/10).","financial_summary":["MACOM Technology Solutions Hold is a large-cap technology business with a $16.1B market cap on $967M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +13% over the past three years and +9% annually across the full decade, the kind of sustained demand persistence that marks a compounder.","Returns on capital run at 12% against a 11% cost of capital, which means the business barely earns its keep economically, with gross margins sitting at 50%.","The business throws off $193M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 20 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders.","Accruals are elevated at -13.8% of assets, and Sloan showed firms building earnings through accruals rather than cash systematically underperform.","On the balance sheet, the balance sheet carries net cash, which is the gold standard: the business never has to make desperate decisions in a bad year, and interest coverage of 24\u00d7 is fortress-like.","Shareholder yield is only 0.3%, a thin return of capital, and insiders hold 6.6% of the shares."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Price sits 319% above estimated fair value \u2014 no margin of safety left, and the cushion against estimate error has been bid away (confirmed by 1 other valuation measure)","sev":"red","cat":"valuation","magnitude":3.191719016949313},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Insiders are net sellers (100% sell ratio, net $9.5M) \u2014 the people closest to the business are reducing their personal stake","sev":"amber","cat":"insider"},{"text":"Technology sector lagging the market significantly, underperforming by 7% over 3 months","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Elevated sector volatility (35% annualized) adds uncertainty","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Above-average market volatility (VIX 26)","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Late-cycle dynamics increase the probability of a slowdown","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Antitrust and platform-regulation risk \u2014 the larger the network effect, the larger the regulatory target on its back, and a single consent decree can reset the moat.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Cybersecurity liability and talent cost inflation \u2014 a single breach can erase years of goodwill, and the war for engineering talent compresses margins even at scale.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Altman Z comfortably in the safe zone \u2014 a fortress balance sheet on this measure"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"MTSI Q4 Earnings Surpass Estimates on Data Center Strength","source":"zacks.com","link":"https://www.zacks.com/stock/news/3025668/mtsi-q4-earnings-surpass-estimates-on-data-center-strength?cid=CS-ZC-FT-analyst_blog%7Cearnings_article-3025668","date":"2026-11-06","timestamp":1793976240.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.494,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"MTSI Q4 Earnings Call Highlights Data Center Growth and Margin Gains","source":"zacks.com","link":"https://www.zacks.com/stock/news/3025577/mtsi-q4-earnings-call-highlights-data-center-growth-and-margin-gains?cid=CS-ZC-FT-analyst_blog_plus%7Cearnings_call_takeaways-3025577","date":"2026-11-06","timestamp":1793973600.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.612,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"What MACOM Technology Solutions (MTS